OL,3,GNEWSAMagical sleuths battled with law
OL,4,Aover witch claims
OL,5,
OL,6,FFears around witchcraft gripped people
OL,7,Fin the 16th and 17th Centuries with
OL,8,Fmany trials leading to the deaths of
OL,9,Fthose accused of casting spells and
OL,10,Fcurses.
OL,12,FMass executions spread throughout
OL,13,FEurope from the early 1500s as
OL,14,F"witchcraft panic" took hold of the
OL,15,Fpublic and historians say tens of
OL,16,Fthousands, mostly women, were executed.
OL,18,FBut research has shown it was not just
OL,19,F"bad witches" who made a pact with the
OL,20,Fdevil to use supernatural powers for
OL,21,Fevil deeds who ended up in the dock.
OL,23,APub: 31-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
